/// @dir include/libchiaking
/// @brief The headers a frontend builds against. The faces at the top are the public API, listed under Public API in the sidebar.

/// @dir include/libchiaking/detail
/// @brief The definitions the faces need, one folder per domain. Reached through the faces and never included directly.

/// @dir include/libchiaking/platform
/// @brief The provider interfaces, the portable default providers and the stock providers built on third-party libraries.

/// @dir include/libchiaking/testing
/// @brief In-memory stores, scripted doubles and conformance suites, for test code only.

/// @dir src
/// @brief The library's implementation.

/// @dir src/core
/// @brief The domains, the PSN and network protocols under them, and the utilities they share. One folder per domain, each split into model, usecases and adapters.

/// @dir src/core/catalog
/// @brief The catalog domain: the cloud list, the owned library, store categories, storefront answers, launch clearance and the fetch state machine.

/// @dir src/core/catalog/model
/// @brief The catalog's values and rules, and its state machines, with no I/O.

/// @dir src/core/catalog/usecases
/// @brief What the catalog does for a caller: listing games, details, launch checks, played games and cache inspection.

/// @dir src/core/catalog/adapters
/// @brief The catalog's links to the outside: PS services, held answers and records on disk, the fetch board and trusted time.

/// @dir src/core/consoles
/// @brief The consoles domain: known consoles, discovery on the local network, pairing at home and over the internet, waking and invitations.

/// @dir src/core/consoles/model
/// @brief The consoles' values and rules, and the pairing state machines.

/// @dir src/core/consoles/usecases
/// @brief What the consoles domain does for a caller: finding, pairing, starting and forgetting consoles.

/// @dir src/core/consoles/adapters
/// @brief The consoles' links to the network, PSN and the console store.

/// @dir src/core/media
/// @brief The media domain: video intake, audio decoding, the microphone encoder and media statistics.

/// @dir src/core/media/adapters
/// @brief The audio decoder, audio output layout and microphone encoder over their codecs.

/// @dir src/core/kakusan
/// @brief The Kakusan domain: sharing a live session with invited players elsewhere.

/// @dir src/core/kakusan/model
/// @brief Kakusan's values, rules and state machines.

/// @dir src/core/kakusan/usecases
/// @brief Hosting a shared session and visiting one as a guest.

/// @dir src/core/kakusan/adapters
/// @brief Kakusan's links to the network, the session being shared and the device store.

/// @dir src/core/messages
/// @brief The messages domain: reading and sending PSN messages.

/// @dir src/core/messages/usecases
/// @brief Talking to PSN's message groups.

/// @dir src/core/play
/// @brief The play domain: starting sessions at home, over the internet and in the cloud, and everything done with a live one.

/// @dir src/core/play/model
/// @brief Session values and rules, start policies and the session state machine.

/// @dir src/core/play/usecases
/// @brief Starting a session in each place and launching in the cloud.

/// @dir src/core/play/adapters
/// @brief The links, media delivery, controllers, seats and cloud launch that drive a live session.

/// @dir src/core/trophies
/// @brief The trophies domain: trophy titles, groups and progress.

/// @dir src/core/trophies/model
/// @brief Trophy values and rules.

/// @dir src/core/trophies/usecases
/// @brief Reading trophy titles and progress for a user.

/// @dir src/core/trophies/adapters
/// @brief The trophy service client and its held answers.

/// @dir src/core/users
/// @brief The users domain: signing in, renewing tokens, saved sign-ins and the calls made as a user.

/// @dir src/core/users/model
/// @brief User values and rules, and the sign-in state machines.

/// @dir src/core/users/usecases
/// @brief Signing users in, renewing them and loading saved ones.

/// @dir src/core/users/adapters
/// @brief The credential store, token caches and the authorised calls made as a user.

/// @dir src/core/psn
/// @brief Clients for PSN's services, used by the domains above.

/// @dir src/core/psn/account
/// @brief The account service client.

/// @dir src/core/psn/auth
/// @brief Sign-in: exchanging an NPSSO or approved code for tokens, and renewing them.

/// @dir src/core/psn/gk
/// @brief The cloud streaming session service: launch specifications, datacenter probes and session allocation.

/// @dir src/core/psn/graphql
/// @brief PSN's GraphQL gateway: persisted queries, the anonymous and app-token clients, and the queries they send.

/// @dir src/core/psn/remote_play
/// @brief Remote play signalling over PSN: push notifications, the notification inbox and holepunch messages.

/// @dir src/core/psn/rest
/// @brief PSN's REST services: accounts, commerce, entitlements, game lists, store, user notifications and more.

/// @dir src/core/net
/// @brief Network protocols and transports below the domains.

/// @dir src/core/net/kakusan
/// @brief Kakusan's wire protocol: control channel, messages, congestion and controller frames.

/// @dir src/core/net/nat
/// @brief Getting through routers: STUN, ICE candidates and PSN holepunch.

/// @dir src/core/net/ntp
/// @brief Trusted time from NTP servers.

/// @dir src/core/net/protocol
/// @brief The streaming protocols: remote play control, Takion and Senkusha.

/// @dir src/core/net/transport
/// @brief The transports: UDP datagrams, RUDP and the HTTP client.

/// @dir src/core/utils
/// @brief Utilities shared by the domains, one job per folder.

/// @dir src/core/utils/bytes
/// @brief Byte reading, writing and encoding.

/// @dir src/core/utils/concurrency
/// @brief Shared flights and other synchronisation helpers.

/// @dir src/core/utils/containers
/// @brief Bounded queues.

/// @dir src/core/utils/diagnostics
/// @brief Logs, the API capture, the HTTP call log and session journals.

/// @dir src/core/utils/json
/// @brief JSON reading and the reply shapes PS services use.

/// @dir src/core/utils/memory
/// @brief Wiping memory and holding secrets.

/// @dir src/core/utils/numeric
/// @brief Checked arithmetic and wrapping sequence numbers.

/// @dir src/core/utils/retry
/// @brief Retrying a call once after renewing its credential.

/// @dir src/core/utils/text
/// @brief Text encoding, UUIDs and string helpers.

/// @dir src/core/utils/timing
/// @brief Deadlines, saturating durations and token buckets.

/// @dir src/platform
/// @brief The stock providers, one folder per capability and one file per operating system or library.

/// @dir src/platform/crypto
/// @brief Crypto providers over OpenSSL, BoringSSL, the console SDK, ARMv8 instructions and micro-ecc.

/// @dir src/platform/curl
/// @brief Shared libcurl transfer handling for the HTTP and WebSocket providers.

/// @dir src/platform/diagnostics
/// @brief System logging for each operating system.

/// @dir src/platform/http
/// @brief The HTTP provider over libcurl.

/// @dir src/platform/net
/// @brief Sockets, polling, DNS and interfaces for each operating system.

/// @dir src/platform/runtime
/// @brief Runtime helpers shared by the providers.

/// @dir src/platform/storage
/// @brief The file-backed record store.

/// @dir src/platform/threading
/// @brief Threads, mutexes and condition variables for each operating system.

/// @dir src/platform/websocket
/// @brief The WebSocket provider over libcurl.
